      "content": "that makes sense, thx. i want to expand on the communication part. in these environments, there's often a very specific way people interact—like using certain slang, a more aggressive tone, or even different body language to show respect or toughness. if i'm trying to design questions that differentiate between someone who grew up in a \"standard\" suburban setting vs someone from one of these high-risk urban areas, what are some of the more distinct linguistic or social cues I should be looking for? like, what are the typical traits that define those \"urban\" communication styles?",
